function SplitModePreview({getValue, md}: RenderPreviewParams) {
  const [html, setHtml] = useState('');
  const theme = useThemeValue();

  const renderPreview = useMemo(() => {
    let timer: number | undefined;
    return () => {
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      timer = window.setTimeout(() => {
        const res = transform(getValue(), {
          allowHTML: md.html,
          breaks: md.breaks,
          linkify: md.linkify,
          linkifyTlds: md.linkifyTlds,
          needToSanitizeHtml: true,
        }).result;
        setHtml(res.html);
      }, 200);
    };
  }, [getValue, md, theme]);

  useEffect(() => {
    renderPreview();
  });

  return <YfmStaticView html={html} mods={{'no-list-reset': true}} />;
}
```

Hmm, `transform(...)` returns `OutputType` where `.result.html` — check OutputType: `{result: {html, meta, ...}, logs}`. The guide used `transform(...).result` then `res.html`, `res.meta`. Wait guide: `const res = transform(getValue(), {...}).result; setHtml(res.html);`. OK.

But careful: `OutputType` — check typings.d.ts lines around 37. It had allowHTML etc. in OptionsType. OutputType shape — let me trust the guide: `.result.html`.

Note `useEffect(() => {renderPreview();})` without deps runs on every render — matches the guide (`[props, render]` deps; render changes when getValue changes... actually getValue identity may be stable). The guide's effect deps `[props, render]` — props changes identity each render probably. To be safe, run effect on every render (no dep array). That matches the intent: each time the editor re-renders the preview component (on doc change), schedule a re-transform.

RenderPreview receives `{getValue, mode, md, directiveSyntax}`. I'll pass the whole params.

